 }
 coords 0 0 0
 m_bRespawnEnabled 0
 m_bWaveRespawn 0
 m_bRallyPointsEnabled 0
 m_iTimeToRespawn 60
 m_iRespawnCutoffMinutes 0
 m_eRespawnMode 0
 m_iTimeLimitMinutes 60
 m_bLockUnusedSlots 1
 m_bUseSafestartTimeLimit 1
 m_iSafestartTimeLimit 15
 m_bUseCVON 1
 m_aMissionDescriptors {
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E1A503377C}" {
   m_sTitle "Mission: Situation"
   m_sTextData "Kolguyev, east coast, 0700. Overcast, calm sea."\
   ""\
   "The beach between Gorshkovo and the naval harbour is the only stretch of open shore on this coast. The Germans have turned it into a strongpoint: a belt of hedgehogs in the shallows and more on the sand, two belts of wire up the slope, a line of Tobruk MG pits, two casemates and two hill bunkers above them, and MG nests covering the south draw and the harbour road. Behind the beach the ground climbs past the mining village of Gorshkovo and its coal silo to the Nadezhda coal mine on the ridge, 1.2 km inland and 200 m up."\
   ""\
   "US infantry are loading into LCVPs at a staging pontoon 850 m offshore."\
   ""\
   "BLUFOR: US Army rifle platoon (1PLT, 1-1 to 1-4, WPNS); the weapons squad has the platoon's engineers and an 81 mm mortar team. Eight LCVPs."\
   "OPFOR: German infantry platoon (ZUG, GRUPPE 1-3, MG-TRUPP). Dug in, no vehicles."
   m_aFactionKeys {
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E1F61769E7}" {
   m_sTitle "BLUFOR Briefing"
   m_sTextData "MISSION"\
   "Destroy the three MCOMs, one per zone. Plant a charge (5 s) on the active MCOM and keep the Germans off it until it blows (45 s). When a zone's MCOM is gone, the next zone opens."\
   ""\
   "ZONES"\
   "1. Beach Red: A on the slope above the middle of the beach, between the two casemates and behind the upper wire."\
   "2. Gorshkovo: B at the coal silo north of the village."\
   "3. Nadezhda mine: C at the conveyor head on the ridge."\
   ""\
   "EXECUTION"\
   "Each element spawns on the pontoon next to its own LCVP: step down into the boat, the squad lead or a volunteer drives. A belt of hedgehogs lies in the shallows off BEACH RED: come in through one of the three cleared lanes (LANE 1-3 on the map) or the boat hangs up short of the beach. The lower wire belt has gaps straight up from each lane, the upper belt has gaps between them. The hedgehogs and dragon's teeth on the sand give some cover. WPNS is 14 strong and takes two boats: its own and the next one north. A spare LCVP waits past the end of the dock."\
   "After safe start the run in takes about two minutes. Mind the rock awash 130 m off the middle of the beach."\
   ""\
   "ENGINEERS (WPNS): four combat engineers, each with a Bangalore torpedo, three satchel charges, an M112 block and a blasting machine. Lay a Bangalore under the wire, then \"Push Bangalore\" to add the next engineer's section; one section won't reach through a belt. Fuse it with the timer or the blasting machine. Satchels are for the bunkers."\
   "MORTAR (WPNS): the 81 mm M1 comes in three loads: the mortar leader carries the base plate, the gunner the tube, the loader the bipod. Set the base plate down (needs the e-tool), then add the bipod and the tube. 14 HE and 2 WP rounds across the team; range tables with the leader and the gunner. Zone 3 is 1.2 km from the beach."\
   ""\
   "When zone 1 falls your spawn moves ashore to the beachhead; when zone 2 falls, to the silo road below the mine."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E199D38E4F}" {
   m_sTitle "OPFOR Briefing"
   m_sTextData "MISSION"\
   "Hold the MCOMs. The Americans will come from the sea. Defuse a planted charge (7 s) before it blows (45 s)."\
   ""\
   "ZONES"\
   "1. Beach Red: A on the slope above the middle of the beach, between the two casemates and behind the upper wire."\
   "2. Gorshkovo: B at the coal silo north of the village."\
   "3. Nadezhda mine: C at the conveyor head on the ridge."\
   ""\
   "EXECUTION"\
   "You start on the slope above the beach. Beach Red is fortified: four Tobruk MG pits behind the upper wire, two casemates (ladder to the roof) and two hill bunkers above them, MG nests at the south draw and on the harbour road. The boats can only get through three lanes in the hedgehog belt. When a zone falls, fall back: your spawn moves to the hill west of Gorshkovo, then to the road behind the mine."\
   "You have no vehicles. Each Gruppe's anti-tank rifleman carries HEAT rifle grenades and bundle charges: use them on the boats."\
   ""\
   "YOU WIN if any MCOM survives the time limit (60 minutes) or the Americans are wiped out."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "OPFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E10A6C267B}" {
   m_sTitle "Administration"
   m_sTextData "Rush, 3 zones x 1 MCOM. Time limit 60 minutes after safe start (safe start max. 15 minutes)."\
   ""\
   "No timed respawns. When a zone falls, every dead player of both sides respawns at their side's new spawn."\
   ""\
   "LCVPs: 8 at the staging pontoon (one per BLUFOR element, two for WPNS, + 1 spare). A destroyed LCVP is respawned at the pontoon for free when the next zone falls; intact boats (beached or adrift) stay where they are. Nothing else respawns."\
   ""\
   "Mission by tanaKa-."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
    "OPFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
 }
 m_iFactionOneRatio 3
 m_iFactionTwoRatio 2
 m_sFactionOneKey "BLU"
 m_sFactionTwoKey "OPF"
